  ---[ end trace a60d797432b656b2 ]---

The gmcc0/gmac1 must be brought in a state in which it doesn't signal a
AG71XX_INT_POLL related status bits as interrupt before registering the
interrupt handler. ag71xx_hw_start will take care of re-initializing the
AG71XX_REG_INT_ENABLE.

Fixes: f529a3742043 ("surprise :p")
Signed-off-by: Sven Eckelmann <sven@narfation.org>

[ Neanderfunk port to the ar71xx ag71xx driver of OpenWrt 19.07
  (target/linux/ar71xx/files/drivers/net/ethernet/atheros/ag71xx/), Linux
  4.14.275, Gluon v2021.1:
  - Same pattern in ar71xx: ag71xx_probe() calls devm_request_irq() long
    before netif_napi_add(). The ath79 fix is ported 1:1 to the same spot
    (after the mac_base ioremap, before platform_get_irq()). The request_irq
    call itself is not moved, as in upstream.
  - Path relative to the kernel root, like the other ag71xx patches in
    patches-4.14 (the files/ tree is copied into the kernel before patching).
  - Note: unlike ath79, the ar71xx platform code (ath79_register_eth() in
    arch/mips/ath79/dev-eth.c) asserts and releases the GMAC reset right
    before platform_device_register(), so a GMAC left running by the
    bootloader should already be quiet here. This patch is a cheap
    safeguard for the case that the interrupt enable bits survive. ]
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/atheros/ag71xx/ag71xx_main.c |    6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/atheros/ag71xx/ag71xx_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/atheros/ag71xx/ag71xx_main.c
@@ -1352,6 +1352,12 @@ static int ag71xx_probe(struct platform_
 	if (!ag->mac_base)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
+	/* ensure that HW is in manual polling mode before interrupts are
+	 * activated. Otherwise ag71xx_interrupt might call napi_schedule
+	 * before it is initialized by netif_napi_add.
+	 */
+	ag71xx_int_disable(ag, AG71XX_INT_POLL);
+
 	dev->irq = platform_get_irq(pdev, 0);
 	err = devm_request_irq(&pdev->dev, dev->irq, ag71xx_interrupt,
 			       0x0, dev_name(&pdev->dev), dev);
